<P STYLE="font: 11pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 24pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: right; border-bottom: black 0.5pt solid"><B>News</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 14pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 3in; text-align: right"><B>FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 11pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 14pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>BMO Announces the Reverse Split of Three Series
of ETNs</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 11pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 11pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white"><B>NEW YORK, March 15, 2024 &ndash; </B>Bank
of Montreal (TSX:BMO)(NYSE:BMO) announced today that it will implement a 1-for-10 reverse split of three series of its outstanding exchange
traded notes, as listed in the table below (the &ldquo;ETNs&rdquo; or &ldquo;Notes&rdquo;), expected to be effective as of March 25, 2024
(the &ldquo;effective date,&rdquo; or the &ldquo;ex date&rdquo;).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 11pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 11pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white">The table below indicates the ETNs that will
be subject to the reverse split, their trading symbols, their current CUSIP numbers, and the CUSIP numbers that they will receive after
giving effect to the reverse split:</P>

<P STYLE="font: 11pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLSPACING="0" CELLPADDING="0" STYLE="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 11pt">
  <TR>
    <TD STYLE="width: 52%; border-bottom: black 1pt solid; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt; background-color: white"><B>ETNs</B></FONT></TD>
    <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; width: 1%; border-bottom: black 1pt solid">&nbsp;</TD>
    <TD STYLE="width: 23%; border-bottom: black 1pt solid; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt; background-color: white"><B>Ticker Symbol</B></FONT></TD>
